    "CXC-PATSUB": {
      "id": "CXC-PATSUB",
      "type_prefix": "CXC",
      "title": "ComposeBus Pattern Subscription & Transport Filtering",
      "domain": "PLT.CIO",
      "source_file": "specs/21-composebus-pattern-subscription.lts",
      "line_range": [
        11,
        16
      ],
      "content_hash": "sha256:b1b9777d0eb9459322ab2d37f0c0b70eafc629451cae31a58753aaef10c4def4",
      "token_count": 131,
      "status": null,
      "properties": {},
      "parent_section": null,
      "document_tag": "SPEC",
      "definition_form": "header"
    },
    "CXC-PS-INTENT": {
      "id": "CXC-PS-INTENT",
      "type_prefix": "CXC",
      "title": "Filter at the Bus, Not the Widget",
      "domain": "PLT.CIO",
      "source_file": "specs/21-composebus-pattern-subscription.lts",
      "line_range": [
        19,
        28
      ],
      "content_hash": "sha256:e52dac592a1e6648ec0ee3f5bb1f4a7334bd7afde60ed8282e656eba632ed5bd",
      "token_count": 234,
      "status": "operational (in-process + MQTT); CAN binding = design, pending a CAN transport.",
      "properties": {
        "definition": "a subscriber registers a namespace *pattern*; the bus delivers only namespaces (and their values) that match. Filtering is the bus's job, transport-side \u2014 never \"deliver everything, let the subscriber discard.\"",
        "rationale": "receive-then-discard is a non-starter on a constrained MCU (it would parse the whole bus to keep 2%). Push the filter as close to the wire as the transport allows.",
        "key-insight": "ComposeBus is a *logical* bus over **pluggable transports** \u2014 in-process, MQTT, and CAN \u2014 so it is **not always CAN**. The subscription primitive is defined once, logically; each transport binding satisfies it natively. The point of this spec is to make the primitive's shape one that *every* transport can push to its own native filter.",
        "status": "operational (in-process + MQTT); CAN binding = design, pending a CAN transport.",
        "part-of": "[SPEC:CXC-PATSUB]"
      },
      "parent_section": "CXC-PATSUB",
      "document_tag": "SPEC",
      "definition_form": "header"
    },
    "CXC-PS-PRIMITIVE": {
      "id": "CXC-PS-PRIMITIVE",
      "type_prefix": "CXC",
      "title": "Trailing-Glob Prefix Subscription",
      "domain": "PLT.CIO",
      "source_file": "specs/21-composebus-pattern-subscription.lts",
      "line_range": [
        31,
        39
      ],
      "content_hash": "sha256:4f4c745d9f59b905667979d7bf091ab920e0fbeb9c004fa85645a9028f861697",
      "token_count": 270,
      "status": null,
      "properties": {
        "as-built": "`ComposeIOBus.subscribe_pattern(pattern, callback)` \u2014 **trailing-glob only**: `prefix/*` matches the prefix and its subtree, `*` matches all; a *mid-pattern* glob raises. The callback receives the *actual member namespace* (not the pattern) and fires per publish (liveness), including family members that appear *after* the subscription was authored.",
        "test": "`subscribe_pattern(\"jumpdrive/*\", cb)` receives every `jumpdrive/...` publish incl. later members; a mid-pattern glob raises; `*` receives all.",
        "part-of": "[SPEC:CXC-PATSUB]"
      },
      "parent_section": "CXC-PATSUB",
      "document_tag": "SPEC",
      "definition_form": "header"
    },
    "CXC-PS-TRANSPORT": {
      "id": "CXC-PS-TRANSPORT",
      "type_prefix": "CXC",
      "title": "One Contract, Native Filtering Per Transport",
      "domain": "PLT.CIO",
      "source_file": "specs/21-composebus-pattern-subscription.lts",
      "line_range": [
        42,
        52
      ],
      "content_hash": "sha256:0d3adb926cd629060fc3ee3281be75fbf8f9ca52f398df352ecf536a23e73d40",
      "token_count": 244,
      "status": null,
      "properties": {
        "principle": "the same logical subscription is filtered at progressively-lower tiers as the transport allows \u2014 memory \u2192 broker \u2192 hardware \u2014 with the subscriber's contract (\"I only get matches\") identical throughout.",
        "test": "the identical `.compose.yaml` subscription produces only-matching delivery over each transport, filtered at that transport's native tier.",
        "part-of": "[SPEC:CXC-PATSUB]"
      },
      "parent_section": "CXC-PATSUB",
      "document_tag": "SPEC",
      "definition_form": "header"
    },
    "CXC-PS-CAN": {
      "id": "CXC-PS-CAN",
      "type_prefix": "CXC",
      "title": "When the Transport Is CAN, the Filter Is a Hardware Mask",
      "domain": "PLT.CIO",
      "source_file": "specs/21-composebus-pattern-subscription.lts",
      "line_range": [
        55,
        67
      ],
      "content_hash": "sha256:e30e3154756aa36ceb445c23d561cfe61fdea7e630cda21fe4c1f5e1e542b80b",
      "token_count": 515,
      "status": null,
      "properties": {
        "definition": "CAN is a broadcast multi-drop bus \u2014 every node sees every frame on the wire \u2014 but every CAN controller has **hardware acceptance filters**: load an arbitration-ID mask and non-matching frames are dropped *by the silicon before they reach the CPU*. A ComposeBus prefix subscription becomes a loaded acceptance mask; the \"I only want this shape\" contract is honored in hardware.",
        "part-of": "[SPEC:CXC-PATSUB]"
      },
